WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.300
1886 — the first recorded XI

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.800
1968 — level after 90

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.100
1999 — two substitutes changed the final

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.600
2008 — won on penalties

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.300
1968 ↔ 2008 — two No. 7s, forty years apart

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.700
Both became champions of Europe.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.700
Both scored in the final.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.700
Both won the Ballon d’Or.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.300
Both peaked in season five.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.200
Eleven days. No margin.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:52.000
1998–99 — three must-wins, every winning goal from the bench

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.000
Three wins. Every winning goal from the bench.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Fergie time — three matches, the same late turn

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Eleven minutes. Six goals. Three turnarounds.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Then the full late-goal record.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:20.300
Only three slipped behind—and all three recovered

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.700
6,028 matches. Pull a thread.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.000
Every claim opens onto the full match record.
